          %title Contents
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#for_waldhausen_categories"} For Waldhausen categories
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related"} Related
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#for_waldhausen_categories_2"} For Waldhausen categories
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#for_waldhausen_infinity1categories_and_stable_infinity1categories"} For Waldhausen (infinity,1)-categories and stable (infinity,1)-categories
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#other"} Other
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The Waldhausen
            = succeed "-construction" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_\bullet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            (as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+space"} infinite loop space
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectrum"} connective spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            equipped with a
            = succeed "." do
              %em Waldhausen structure
          %p The construction can take as input any of the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} Waldhausen (infinity,1)-category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+derivator"} stable derivator
            %li …
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#for_waldhausen_categories For Waldhausen categories
          %p
            Recall from the definition at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            that the K-theory spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the diagonal simplicial set on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Core(Func(\Delta^n,C))
            of sequences of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and equivalences between these (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+space"} Segal space
            induced by
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The Waldhausen S-construction mimics precisely this: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
            for every integer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            define a simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n C'
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of the category whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                objects are sequences
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \hookrightarrow A_{0,1} \hookrightarrow \cdots \hookrightarrow A_{0,n}
                of Waldhausen cofibrations;
              %ul
                %li
                  together with choices of quotients
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{i j} = A_{0, j}/ A_{0,i}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{0,i} \to A_{0,j} \to A_{i j}
            %li
              %p
                morphisms are collections of morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{A_{i,j} \to B_{i,j}\}
                that commute with all diagrams in sight.
          %p
            Then one finds that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} realization
            of the bisimplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mo •
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_\bullet C'
            with respect to one variable is itself naturally a topological
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mo •
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{(n)}_\bullet C'
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} topological realization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{K}(C)_n = |S^{(n)}_\bullet C'|
          %p
            this is the
            %strong S-construction
            of the
            %strong
              Waldhausen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
              spectrum
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
          %p (… roughly at least, need to polish this, see link below meanwhile…)
