          %h3#other Other
          %p A combinatorial construction of symmetries due to Nadler has a relation to the S-construction in a special case:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"}> David Nadler
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Cyclic symmetries of
                  = succeed "-quiver" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.0070"} arxiv/1306.0070
          %blockquote
            %p This short note contains a combinatorial construction of symmetries arising in symplectic geometry (partially wrapped or infinitesimal Fukaya categories), algebraic geometry (derived categories of singularities), and K-theory (Waldhausen’s S-construction). Our specific motivation (in the spirit of expectations of Kontsevich, and to be taken up in general elsewhere) is a combinatorial construction of quantizations of Lagrangian skeleta (equivalent to microlocal sheaves in their many guises). We explain here the one dimensional case of ribbon graphs where the main result of this paper gives an immediate solution.
          %p
            Interpretation in terms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorified+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} categorified Dold-Kan correspondence
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Dyckerhoff17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Dyckerhoff"}> Tobias Dyckerhoff
              ,
              %em A categorified Dold-Kan correspondence
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.08356"}> arXiv:1710.08356
              )
